#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:273
msgid "Getting One Key Directly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:275
msgid "When only one key is needed, call the corresponding launcher helper:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:277
msgid ""
"let l1_key = my_kernels::copy(\n"
"    cutile::api::meta::<f32>(&[1024]).partition([128]),\n"
"    cutile::api::meta::<f32>(&[1024]),\n"
")\n"
".generics(vec![\"f32\".into(), \"128\".into()])\n"
".l1_cache_key()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:286
msgid "Or derive the L2 key directly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:288
msgid ""
"let l2_key = my_kernels::copy(\n"
"    cutile::api::meta::<f32>(&[1024]).partition([128]),\n"
"    cutile::api::meta::<f32>(&[1024]),\n"
")\n"
".generics(vec![\"f32\".into(), \"128\".into()])\n"
".l2_cache_key()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:297
msgid ""
"`l1_cache_key()` returns the complete structured `TileFunctionKey`, not the "
"shortened `display_hash()` debug label. `l2_cache_key()` returns the 64-"
"character lowercase SHA-256 used by the persistent cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:299
msgid ""
"Each terminal consumes its launcher. If both keys are needed, resolve the "
"launch specialization once instead of constructing the launcher twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:301
msgid "Getting Both Keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:303
msgid ""
"`specialize()` resolves the specialization identity for this launch without "
"compiling or launching the kernel. It materializes the launch inputs and "
"returns a `Specialization` containing the complete L1 key and a lazy module "
"AST provider:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:305
msgid ""
"let specialization = my_kernels::copy(\n"
"    cutile::api::meta::<f32>(&[1024]).partition([128]),\n"
"    cutile::api::meta::<f32>(&[1024]),\n"
")\n"
".generics(vec![\"f32\".into(), \"128\".into()])\n"
".specialize()?;\n"
"\n"
"let l1_key = specialization.l1_cache_key().clone();\n"
"let l2_key = specialization.l2_cache_key()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:317
msgid ""
"`Specialization::l1_cache_key()` only borrows an already resolved key, so it "
"returns `&TileFunctionKey` rather than `Result`. `specialize()` may fail "
"while materializing launch inputs, and `l2_cache_key()` may fail while "
"running the compiler frontend or serializing bytecode, so those calls use `?"
"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:319
msgid "Matching the Real L2 Lookup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:321
msgid ""
"L2 derivation runs the compiler frontend and serializes Tile IR because the "
"persistent key hashes the frontend output. The helper and the real disk-"
"cache lookup share the same bytecode-to-key function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:323
msgid ""
"launcher.l2_cache_key()\n"
"    ↓\n"
"Specialization::l2_cache_key()\n"
"    ↓\n"
"KernelCompiler::l2_cache_key()\n"
"    ├── compiler frontend\n"
"    ├── Tile IR bytecode serialization\n"
"    ▼\n"
"current_l2_key_for_bytecode()\n"
"    ▼\n"
"l2_key(...)\n"
"\n"
"compile_bytecode_cached()\n"
"    ▼\n"
"current_l2_key_for_bytecode()\n"
"    ▼\n"
"l2_key(...)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:343
msgid ""
"The bytecode version comes from the serializer. Launcher helpers resolve the "
"target from the launch device; compile-only callers configure it on "
"`KernelCompiler`. The default optimization level and current `tileiras` "
"fingerprint are resolved internally. This makes the helper return the exact "
"L2 key that the JIT would query."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:345
msgid "Work Performed by the Helpers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:347
msgid ""
"Both launcher helpers materialize upstream `DeviceOp` inputs to derive "
"strides and specialization hints. An arbitrary upstream operation may "
"perform device work during that step; cache tooling can use `api::meta` "
"inputs to provide tensor metadata without allocating device storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:349
msgid "After input materialization:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:351
msgid ""
"L1 derivation does not construct the module AST or run the compiler frontend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:352
msgid ""
"L2 derivation constructs the AST, runs the frontend, and serializes bytecode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:353
msgid ""
"Neither helper reads or writes a `JitStore`, runs the target-kernel "
"`tileiras` backend, loads a CUDA module, or populates the L1 cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:355
msgid ""
"The `_on` variants (`specialize_on`, `l1_cache_key_on`, and "
"`l2_cache_key_on`) select the device from an explicit stream instead of the "
"default device policy. All of these APIs derive keys only; callers remain "
"responsible for `JitStore::contains`, `delete`, cache seeding, and prewarm "
"orchestration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:357
msgid "Compile-Only API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:359
msgid ""
"Most users compile kernels by launching a generated `#[cutile::entry]` "
"launcher. cuTile also exposes `cutile::compile_api::KernelCompiler` for pre-"
"compilation and other compile-only workflows that need Tile IR text or "
"bytecode without launching a kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:361
msgid ""
"use cutile::compile_api::KernelCompiler;\n"
"\n"
"let artifacts = KernelCompiler::new(my_kernels::__module_ast_self, "
"\"my_kernels\", \"tile_math\")\n"
"    .generics(vec![\"32\".into()])\n"
"    .strides(&[(\"output\", &[1])])\n"
"    .target(\"sm_80\")\n"
"    .compile()?;\n"
"\n"
"let ir_text = artifacts.ir_text();\n"
"let bytecode = artifacts.bytecode()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:374
msgid ""
"For cache tooling that only needs the persistent key, use the same builder "
"with `l2_cache_key()`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:376
msgid ""
"let l2_key = KernelCompiler::new(my_kernels::__module_ast_self, "
"\"my_kernels\", \"tile_math\")\n"
"    .generics(vec![\"32\".into()])\n"
"    .strides(&[(\"output\", &[1])])\n"
"    .target(\"sm_80\")\n"
"    .l2_cache_key()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:384
msgid ""
"This runs the frontend and the canonical bytecode serializer but does not "
"compile a cubin or access the configured `JitStore`. The target comes from `."
"target(...)`; the bytecode version, default optimization level, and current "
"`tileiras` fingerprint are selected internally. Advanced tools that "
"intentionally model another toolchain can continue to call the lower-level "
"`jit_cache::l2_key(...)` with explicit inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:386
msgid ""
"`KernelCompiler` takes the same specialization information that a launcher "
"normally infers from its arguments: entry-function generics, tensor stride "
"and specialization hints, scalar hints, target architecture, optional "
"constant grid, and compile options. Use it for pre-compilation pipelines, "
"tooling, tests, and CPU-only validation of generated IR or bytecode. The `."
"target(\"sm_...\")` value supplies the target architecture explicitly "
"because there is no active CUDA device in compile-only mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:388
msgid ""
"Compile-only pre-compilation is separate from the launch-time JIT cache. "
"`KernelCompiler` returns artifacts for the specialization you describe; it "
"does not allocate tensors, launch CUDA work, insert a compiled function into "
"the process-local JIT cache, or produce a host-side result value. A later "
"call through the generated launcher still performs the normal cache lookup "
"and may compile on first launch unless that launch path is taught to consume "
"the precompiled artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:390
msgid "Inspecting Compiler Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:392
msgid ""
"Two entry attributes are honored for inspection. `print_ir = true` prints "
"the generated entry wrapper, the source kernel, and the compiled Tile IR "
"text during JIT compilation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:394
msgid ""
"#[cutile::entry(print_ir = true)]\n"
"fn debug_kernel<const S: [i32; 2]>(...) { ... }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:399
msgid "`dump_mlir_dir` writes the compiled Tile IR text to files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:401
msgid ""
"#[cutile::entry(dump_mlir_dir = \"/tmp/cutile-ir\")]\n"
"fn debug_kernel<const S: [i32; 2]>(...) { ... }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:406
msgid ""
"There is no attribute for substituting hand-edited IR: the compiler always "
"assembles its own output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:408
msgid ""
"The `CUTILE_DUMP` and `CUTILE_DUMP_FILTER` environment variables print the "
"compiler's output to stderr, once per compiled module:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:56
msgid "Variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:56
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:56
msgid "`CUTILE_DUMP`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:56
msgid ""
"Comma-separated stages: `ir` (the Tile IR module as text), `bytecode` or "
"`bc` (the encoded image, decoded back to text), or `all` for both. These are "
"the only stages emitted today; the pass-level names `ast`, `resolved`, "
"`typed`, and `instantiated` are accepted but produce no output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:56
msgid "`CUTILE_DUMP_FILTER`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:56
msgid ""
"Comma-separated `module::function` paths or bare function names. The dumps "
"are per module, so a qualified entry selects by its module part (`kernels::"
"fmha_prefill` dumps every kernel compiled from `kernels`); a bare function "
"name matches every module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:415
msgid "`TILE_IR_DUMP=1` is a legacy alias for `CUTILE_DUMP=ir`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:417
msgid "Bytecode Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:419
msgid ""
"The compiler can write Tile IR bytecode at versions 13.2 and 13.3, and picks "
"one per toolchain so that a newer default is never handed to an older "
"`tileiras`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:421
msgid ""
"`CUTILE_BYTECODE_VERSION`, when set (e.g. `13.2`), overrides everything else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:422
msgid ""
"Otherwise the resolved toolkit's `cuda.h` decides: CUDA 13.2 emits 13.2, "
"CUDA 13.3 and newer emit 13.3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:423
msgid ""
"Otherwise — `CUTILE_TILEIRAS_PATH` pointing at a bare binary, or `tileiras` "
"found on `PATH` — the compiler probes the binary with a small representative "
"kernel at each version, newest first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:425
msgid ""
"The result is clamped to the emittable range. A toolkit older than CUDA "
"13.2, or a probe that cannot run (the temporary directory is not writable, "
"the binary cannot be launched or crashes, or it rejects every version), is a "
"compile error naming the cause rather than a silent fallback. The selected "
"version is part of the persistent cache key, and `CompileArtifacts::"
"bytecode()` writes the same negotiated version a launch would use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/jit-compilation.md:427
msgid "Compilation Failures"
msgstr ""

